.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_INPUT_NEW 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_input_new ,
.Nm dtfl_input_to_stream ,
.Nm dtfl_input_send ,
.Nm dtfl_input_flush ,
.Nm dtfl_input_advance_to ,
.Nm dtfl_input_time ,
.Nm dtfl_input_close
.Nd supply records to a timely dataflow interactively
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely_ops.h
.Ft dtfl_input *
.Fn dtfl_input_new "const dtfl_type *type"
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_input_to_stream "dtfl_input *in" "dtfl_scope *scope"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_input_send "dtfl_input *in" "const void *rec" "size_t len"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_input_flush "dtfl_input *in"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_input_advance_to "dtfl_input *in" "const uint64_t *t"
.Ft const uint64_t *
.Fn dtfl_input_time "const dtfl_input *in"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_input_close "dtfl_input *in"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A
.Vt dtfl_input
is a handle through which the caller feeds records into a running
computation, the C form of timely's
.Vt InputHandle .
.Fn dtfl_input_new
allocates one for records of
.Fa type ,
which it retains.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_input_to_stream
registers the handle with
.Fa scope
and returns the resulting input
.Vt dtfl_stream .
The scope's time class must be totally ordered.
A handle may be attached to several scopes; each attachment is a
separate input operator fed by the same handle, so a record sent after
one attachment is not seen by an operator that attached earlier (the
handle flushes buffered records when a new stream registers).
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_input_send
buffers a record at the handle's current epoch.
.Fn dtfl_input_flush
pushes any buffered records to the attached streams at the current
epoch; buffering also flushes automatically once it reaches an internal
threshold.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_input_advance_to
closes the current epoch, flushing it, and opens a new one at
.Fa t ,
a time of the scope's class.
Advancing lets timely issue progress notifications, because the input
can no longer produce records at an earlier time.
.Fn dtfl_input_time
returns the current epoch, or
.Dv NULL
if no stream has been created yet.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_input_close
seals the input, closing its final epoch, and frees the handle.
After it returns, the handle must not be used.
Closing is what lets the dataflow drain and shut down; a program that
never closes an input and never drops the capability it implies will
step forever.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_input_new
returns a new handle.
.Fn dtfl_input_to_stream
returns the input stream.
.Fn dtfl_input_time
returns the current epoch, or
.Dv NULL
before the first
.Fn dtfl_input_to_stream .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dtfl_input *in = dtfl_input_new(dtfl_type_u64());
dtfl_probe *p = dtfl_probe_new();
/* inside the build callback: */
dtfl_stream *s = dtfl_input_to_stream(in, scope);
dtfl_stream_probe_with(s, p);

for (uint64_t round = 0; round < 10; round++) {
	unsigned char buf[8];
	uint64_t next = round + 1;
	dtfl_put_u64(buf, round);
	dtfl_input_send(in, buf, sizeof buf);
	dtfl_input_advance_to(in, &next);
	while (dtfl_probe_less_than(p, &next))
		dtfl_worker_step(w);
}
dtfl_input_close(in);
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
.Fn dtfl_input_advance_to
calls the panic hook if
.Fa t
does not advance the current epoch, and
.Fn dtfl_input_to_stream
calls it if the scope's time class is not totally ordered; both are
contract violations.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_probe_new 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_unordered_input_new 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_worker_dataflow 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
These are the C forms of timely's
.Vt InputHandle
and the
.Fn new_input ,
.Fn input_from
and
.Fn to_stream
methods of the
.Vt Input
trait.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
A
.Vt dtfl_input
belongs to the thread that runs the worker it feeds and must not be
used from another thread (PLAN section 5).
Send, advance and close all run on that thread.
